WEBVTT

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:26.020
How can I tell you this?

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:37.140
How can I tell you this?

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:47.620
I cannot touch you

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:54.260
But I...

00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:58.490
...can kill you

00:01:01.130 --> 00:01:05.610
I'm so sad to say to you...

00:01:05.610 --> 00:01:10.540
...but don't put your face so close to me.

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:16.020
Now I hear you say my name...

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:25.050
...so I cross the light to be with you

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:43.940
Huh?

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:48.440
Where am I?

00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:51.940
Don't you think so?

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:53.310
I do, I do.

00:01:53.450 --> 00:01:54.820
Isn't that funny?

00:01:54.950 --> 00:01:56.850
Tell me about it.

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:00.490
Oh, yeah. I have to go to school.

00:02:02.330 --> 00:02:08.200
Journey of the Heart.

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:05.180
HIGH
SCHOOL

00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:13.010
Good morning.

00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:15.310
Oh, Miyuki. Morning!

00:02:15.310 --> 00:02:17.880
Sawako, you cut your hair.

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:19.640
Yeah, yesterday.

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:22.080
You really cut it all off.

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:23.850
Sawako, did you get your heart broken?

00:02:23.850 --> 00:02:24.420
Oh, but it's not like I got my heart broken.
Sawako, did you get your heart broken?

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:26.610
Oh, but it's not like I got my heart broken.

00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:29.220
But it looks good.

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:30.160
Yeah, it's cute.

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:30.360
Thanks.
Yeah, it's cute.

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:31.290
Thanks.

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:34.030
Maybe I'll get my hair cut too.

00:02:34.030 --> 00:02:36.320
Tell me which salon you went to.

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:37.800
Sure.

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:39.590
Oh, wait for me.

00:02:41.330 --> 00:02:42.900
Did you bring the origami paper?

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:44.370
Of course.

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:49.340
Odd... Something seems different.

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:57.680
Here you are.

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:03.390
NOW SELLING
Purchase Tickets Here

00:03:09.230 --> 00:03:10.930
Hmm...

00:03:10.930 --> 00:03:12.600
Okay, the pork cutlet bowl!

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:15.490
Pork Cutlet Bowl

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:15.490
Huh?

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:17.530
It's stuck.

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:25.710
NOW SELLING
Purchase Tickets Here

00:03:19.370 --> 00:03:20.910
What are you having?

00:03:20.910 --> 00:03:22.980
Good question.

00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:24.940
Hey, it's lit up.

00:03:24.940 --> 00:03:25.710
For real?

00:03:25.710 --> 00:03:26.250
For real?

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:28.410
Lucky me. Pork cutlet bowl!

00:03:28.650 --> 00:03:31.380
What? Hey!

00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:34.490
That's cheating.

00:03:34.490 --> 00:03:36.090
But why?

00:03:35.590 --> 00:03:44.820
PLEASE TAKE
YOUR TICKET
TO THE COUNTER

00:03:40.430 --> 00:03:44.560
Oh, well. I don't think I'm that hungry anyway.

00:04:05.990 --> 00:04:07.620
Matsumoto-senpai?

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:09.190
Hmm?

00:04:09.190 --> 00:04:12.620
May I make a recording of you
playing sometime?

00:04:13.030 --> 00:04:15.090
What? But why?

00:04:15.090 --> 00:04:19.620
Actually, I want to listen to you
play the piano at home too.

00:04:20.270 --> 00:04:21.320
Sure.

00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:35.350
Matsumoto-senpai?

00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:43.810
Does that mean he doesn't
even want to look at me?

00:04:53.870 --> 00:04:56.330
What the? It won't open.

00:04:56.800 --> 00:04:58.270
How come?

00:05:00.740 --> 00:05:02.740
Now I remember...

00:05:01.770 --> 00:05:05.340
<i>MUSIC</i>
<i>ROOM</i>

00:05:06.010 --> 00:05:10.710
Don't worry. I'm sure
Senior Matsumoto likes you, too.

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:12.690
You really think so?

00:05:12.690 --> 00:05:14.790
Ask him if he'd like to walk home
from school with us.

00:05:14.790 --> 00:05:17.920
I'll casually excuse myself partway.

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:19.030
What?

00:05:19.030 --> 00:05:20.490
Go on.

00:05:41.350 --> 00:05:42.750
Sakura?!

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:46.440
Uh, oh. For real?

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:06.930
But why?

00:06:11.380 --> 00:06:15.070
He never said anything about having a girlfriend.

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:24.950
I hate this.

00:06:31.900 --> 00:06:33.230
I'm...

00:06:36.340 --> 00:06:37.890
I'm...

00:06:54.090 --> 00:06:55.990
Welcome back, Sakura.

00:06:57.220 --> 00:06:58.780
Who are you?

00:06:59.360 --> 00:07:01.490
REAPER
#A-100100

00:06:59.990 --> 00:07:03.290
Reaper Number 100100.

00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:06.530
But you can call me Momo.

00:07:06.530 --> 00:07:07.870
Momo?

00:07:07.870 --> 00:07:09.570
Note: Momo means "Peach" and Sakura means "Cherry"

00:07:07.870 --> 00:07:11.440
Momo and Sakura, what a good combination!

00:07:11.440 --> 00:07:14.700
Wait, did you say reaper?!

00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:17.910
That is how I introduced myself.

00:07:17.910 --> 00:07:20.780
Wait, you're kidding! Am I dead?!

00:07:20.780 --> 00:07:23.340
Did you go and kill yourself
and then forget about it?

00:07:23.820 --> 00:07:27.950
What?! No, uh, I...

00:07:28.890 --> 00:07:30.790
I only thought that I hated this...

00:07:31.520 --> 00:07:35.430
...but while I was looking down,
I had a feeling I was being sucked in...

00:07:35.430 --> 00:07:37.450
...and then I felt like I was flying...

00:07:37.700 --> 00:07:40.130
See? You jumped to your death.

00:07:40.130 --> 00:07:41.300
I did not!

00:07:41.300 --> 00:07:42.740
Yes, you did.

00:07:42.740 --> 00:07:44.300
Be quiet, black cat!

00:07:44.300 --> 00:07:45.840
The name's Daniel.

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:48.540
Is this a dream? This has to be a dream.

00:07:48.540 --> 00:07:49.880
It is not a dream.

00:07:49.880 --> 00:07:52.480
I'll prove it. Try jumping off the ledge.

00:07:52.480 --> 00:07:54.470
I'll die if I do that!

00:07:54.950 --> 00:07:57.010
Okay, then try jumping up.

00:07:57.150 --> 00:07:58.980
That's impossible!

00:07:58.980 --> 00:08:00.110
Wh-whoa!

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:03.090
What's happening to me?! Eek!

00:08:03.860 --> 00:08:06.720
There, there. Calm down, Sakura.

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:10.730
I don't know why, but it really impressed me.

00:08:10.730 --> 00:08:13.500
Am I really dead?

00:08:13.500 --> 00:08:18.500
It's okay. I always make sure to
take away the souls of the dead.

00:08:18.500 --> 00:08:20.670
There's nothing okay about it!

00:08:20.670 --> 00:08:22.170
Shall we go?

00:08:22.170 --> 00:08:23.700
What? Go?

00:08:26.180 --> 00:08:29.650
N... No thanks! I respectfully decline your offer!

00:08:29.650 --> 00:08:32.880
That is what they call poor sportsmanship.

00:08:33.420 --> 00:08:35.250
That's easy for you to say.

00:08:36.820 --> 00:08:39.290
Do I have to go?

00:08:41.260 --> 00:08:42.920
Really for real?

00:08:47.070 --> 00:08:49.470
It doesn't feel cold anymore.

00:08:51.400 --> 00:08:52.400
Okay...

00:08:52.400 --> 00:08:53.890
What is it?

00:08:54.610 --> 00:08:56.910
At least let me say goodbye to everyone.

00:08:57.580 --> 00:08:57.980
You're up next. You can do it!

00:08:57.980 --> 00:08:59.480
One last time.
You're up next. You can do it!

00:08:59.480 --> 00:09:00.100
You're up next. You can do it!

00:09:00.950 --> 00:09:04.110
I think it's faster to fly than walk.

00:09:04.680 --> 00:09:06.480
I want to walk.

00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:12.420
What are you doing?

00:09:14.260 --> 00:09:15.660
Eek!

00:09:21.530 --> 00:09:24.170
Nobody can see you...

00:09:24.170 --> 00:09:26.000
...so they will run into you without thinking twice.

00:09:26.810 --> 00:09:31.240
And every time they do, you'll feel
like your life is being shortened.

00:09:31.240 --> 00:09:33.210
I don't have a life to shorten, now do I?!

00:09:33.680 --> 00:09:35.750
Ugh. She criticized me.

00:09:35.750 --> 00:09:39.240
I'll fly. I'll fly if it gets you off my back. I'll fly!

00:09:44.960 --> 00:09:47.260
This is the city where you lived.

00:09:47.560 --> 00:09:49.030
Wow...

00:09:49.800 --> 00:09:54.100
What? Where I "lived"? You're using past tense.

00:09:54.630 --> 00:09:57.530
I believe that it's important
to use proper grammar.

00:09:58.840 --> 00:10:00.840
Hey, that house...

00:10:00.840 --> 00:10:03.330
That's where Yamanoshita lived.
I had a crush on him in middle school.

00:10:04.280 --> 00:10:07.610
Oh, and that white building
is the hospital where I was born.

00:10:08.610 --> 00:10:12.610
What's the use of being a tour guide if there
aren't any real attractions?

00:10:13.050 --> 00:10:17.320
This city is overflowing
with your memories of the past.

00:10:18.560 --> 00:10:21.360
My memories of the past?

00:10:24.130 --> 00:10:26.120
What's that house?

00:10:27.630 --> 00:10:29.170
That's...

00:10:29.170 --> 00:10:33.000
KOSAKAI

00:10:31.300 --> 00:10:33.000
...my home.

00:10:49.960 --> 00:10:51.920
Hello, this is the Kosakai residence.

00:10:53.560 --> 00:10:55.050
Yes...

00:10:56.460 --> 00:10:57.030
That's right. Don't worry.

00:10:57.030 --> 00:10:58.230
Mom...
That's right. Don't worry.

00:10:58.230 --> 00:10:59.990
That's right. Don't worry.

00:11:03.040 --> 00:11:07.500
Mom's smiling even though I died.

00:11:07.910 --> 00:11:09.870
Yes, all right then...

00:11:10.640 --> 00:11:12.370
Hey, we can go inside.

00:11:15.750 --> 00:11:18.650
It must be useful being able to do this.

00:11:18.650 --> 00:11:19.510
I suppose.

00:11:23.190 --> 00:11:24.520
I'm home.

00:11:25.460 --> 00:11:26.430
Hello, dear.

00:11:26.430 --> 00:11:28.230
I'm so ticked off.

00:11:28.230 --> 00:11:29.190
What is it?

00:11:29.190 --> 00:11:32.250
The boys told me I looked fat.

00:11:33.400 --> 00:11:35.300
But they could be right.

00:11:35.300 --> 00:11:36.430
What?!

00:11:36.940 --> 00:11:39.340
Wash your hands. We'll have tea.

00:11:39.340 --> 00:11:40.810
Sure.

00:11:42.010 --> 00:11:43.780
What day is it today?

00:11:43.780 --> 00:11:45.280
The 4th.

00:11:45.280 --> 00:11:48.480
I jumped off the bridge on the 1st...

00:11:48.480 --> 00:11:50.680
...so it's only been 3 days since I died.

00:11:51.950 --> 00:11:54.020
Your calculation is correct.

00:11:54.020 --> 00:11:57.460
Both Mom and Ayame are already over it.

00:11:58.690 --> 00:12:01.690
They're eating snacks without me...

00:12:01.690 --> 00:12:04.690
...smiling, and getting fat, all without me.

00:12:10.140 --> 00:12:12.540
I can't feel my butt.

00:12:17.240 --> 00:12:19.640
I feel like if I rolled off the bed, I wouldn't fall.

00:12:21.010 --> 00:12:23.380
Are you done with your goodbyes?

00:12:23.380 --> 00:12:24.310
Not yet.

00:12:25.850 --> 00:12:27.280
Hey, is that true?

00:12:27.920 --> 00:12:31.860
Even Sawako and Miyuki
seem perfectly fine without me.
It's true. He said so himself.

00:12:31.860 --> 00:12:33.260
Even Sawako and Miyuki
seem perfectly fine without me.
What?

00:12:33.930 --> 00:12:34.990
Do I no longer have a place in this world?

00:12:34.990 --> 00:12:37.460
Do I no longer have a place in this world?
But that's so...

00:12:37.460 --> 00:12:37.830
Yeah, she's gonna freak out for sure.

00:12:37.830 --> 00:12:39.260
Hey, she's getting depressed.
Yeah, she's gonna freak out for sure.

00:12:39.770 --> 00:12:44.440
There's no point in getting
depressed now. Cheer up.

00:12:44.440 --> 00:12:46.570
There's no point to cheering up either.

00:12:46.570 --> 00:12:49.840
All right, let's go somewhere
that's bound to cheer you up.

00:12:49.840 --> 00:12:51.340
What?

00:12:50.440 --> 00:12:52.400
Matsumoto

00:12:53.880 --> 00:12:56.720
This is where I'm supposed to cheer up?

00:12:56.720 --> 00:12:59.980
Yeah. Isn't this the room of the boy you like?

00:13:00.520 --> 00:13:03.660
Uh, well, you see, I'm in this mess
in the first place...

00:13:03.660 --> 00:13:06.390
...because I was rejected by Senior Matsumoto.

00:13:07.060 --> 00:13:11.230
To be more precise, you were shot down
before you had the chance to be rejected.

00:13:11.230 --> 00:13:13.530
You don't need to be that precise.

00:13:20.510 --> 00:13:23.340
Senior Matsumoto on the piano.

00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:29.550
Maybe this is for the best after all.

00:13:38.320 --> 00:13:40.290
I'm kind of tired.

00:13:41.390 --> 00:13:43.990
How long do we have to keep this up?

00:13:46.270 --> 00:13:48.430
I should get going.

00:13:49.170 --> 00:13:49.930
Hmm?

00:13:50.940 --> 00:13:55.530
My past wasn't anything that special after all.

00:13:57.010 --> 00:14:00.450
After all, everyone seems to be fine without me.

00:14:02.850 --> 00:14:06.580
Normally, people jump off bridges
after that sort of revelation.

00:14:07.420 --> 00:14:10.220
It's unusual to start thinking that
after the deed is done.

00:14:11.120 --> 00:14:15.220
I made the correct choice in my subconscious.

00:14:15.560 --> 00:14:20.970
Do you think so? Is what you think
is correct actually correct?

00:14:20.970 --> 00:14:22.430
What?

00:14:23.040 --> 00:14:25.030
Let's look a little harder.

00:14:29.940 --> 00:14:31.410
Thank you for the food.

00:14:40.920 --> 00:14:42.720
There's a bowl for me.

00:14:43.960 --> 00:14:44.920
It's good.

00:14:44.920 --> 00:14:46.190
Isn't it?

00:14:46.190 --> 00:14:48.850
But I'm getting tired of having
pork cutlet bowl every day.

00:14:50.830 --> 00:14:54.370
I know, but I have a feeling that
if I keep making this...

00:14:54.370 --> 00:14:57.840
...Sakura will come back to us.

00:14:57.840 --> 00:14:59.600
I'm good with this.

00:15:01.340 --> 00:15:04.210
Okay, then could you at least make it
with something besides pork?

00:15:04.980 --> 00:15:07.450
You must really like pork cutlets.

00:15:07.950 --> 00:15:09.280
Yeah.

00:15:14.490 --> 00:15:16.320
Matsumoto...

00:15:15.690 --> 00:15:18.160
KOSAKAI

00:15:16.320 --> 00:15:18.160
I'm sorry for coming so late at night.

00:15:19.220 --> 00:15:22.530
I brought the recording.

00:15:22.530 --> 00:15:24.300
Thank you.

00:15:24.300 --> 00:15:27.060
It's all right. You don't have to feel responsible.

00:15:27.700 --> 00:15:31.140
But I promised Sakura she could have this.

00:15:31.900 --> 00:15:33.960
I'm sorry that there isn't any more I can do.

00:15:34.970 --> 00:15:37.610
I'll let her listen to it right away.

00:15:37.610 --> 00:15:41.140
Thank you. I'm sorry for the intrusion.

00:15:57.630 --> 00:16:01.930
He remembered what I asked him for.

00:16:02.900 --> 00:16:06.130
KANNAGI
CRAM
SCHOOL

00:16:20.490 --> 00:16:22.150
We've made a lot.

00:16:22.850 --> 00:16:24.340
Yeah.

00:16:26.020 --> 00:16:28.690
Let's keep going until we get to 1,000.

00:16:29.900 --> 00:16:31.620
After all, this is for Sakura.

00:16:53.250 --> 00:16:55.480
Hey, wait up!

00:16:57.360 --> 00:16:58.850
Sakura?

00:16:59.990 --> 00:17:01.460
...to die.

00:17:01.460 --> 00:17:02.990
What?

00:17:02.990 --> 00:17:04.660
I don't want to die!

00:17:05.460 --> 00:17:07.060
I want to be alive!

00:17:08.570 --> 00:17:12.340
There's nothing that special about me...

00:17:12.340 --> 00:17:15.310
...and I got rejected by the boy I like...

00:17:15.310 --> 00:17:18.140
...and my favorite food
is boring old pork cutlets...

00:17:18.140 --> 00:17:22.140
...and I feel totally pathetic now, but...

00:17:23.320 --> 00:17:25.150
But... but...

00:17:26.080 --> 00:17:27.880
I want to stay alive!

00:17:34.990 --> 00:17:36.590
Okay, then do that.

00:17:37.430 --> 00:17:39.090
What?

00:17:40.430 --> 00:17:41.200
Are you sure?

00:17:41.200 --> 00:17:54.100
REAPER
LOAN

00:17:41.630 --> 00:17:42.530
Sure.

00:17:42.530 --> 00:17:43.940
Really?!

00:17:43.940 --> 00:17:45.300
Uh-huh.

00:17:45.300 --> 00:17:48.540
Can I really come back to life?!

00:17:48.540 --> 00:17:50.040
Probably.

00:17:50.640 --> 00:17:53.550
But don't reapers need to take souls away?

00:17:54.950 --> 00:17:58.120
You're sure that you want to
bring me back to life?

00:17:58.120 --> 00:18:00.490
Actually, the fact of the matter is...

00:18:00.490 --> 00:18:02.420
Kosakai,

00:18:12.430 --> 00:18:14.230
You're not dead yet.

00:18:14.870 --> 00:18:16.740
Something went wrong...

00:18:16.740 --> 00:18:19.500
...and your soul went walkabout
for some reason.

00:18:20.010 --> 00:18:21.210
What?

00:18:21.210 --> 00:18:25.910
Daniel was being mean
and poking fun at you at first...

00:18:26.880 --> 00:18:30.510
...but I never said a word about you being dead.

00:18:32.420 --> 00:18:35.410
Well, I'll be. I'm alive after all.

00:18:37.060 --> 00:18:38.450
I'm alive?

00:18:39.220 --> 00:18:41.360
You took a light blow to the head.

00:18:41.360 --> 00:18:43.200
Your brainwaves are normal...

00:18:43.200 --> 00:18:46.060
...so they're waiting for you
to regain consciousness.

00:18:46.060 --> 00:18:47.770
Oh, I see.

00:18:47.770 --> 00:18:49.430
Now, go back.

00:18:51.140 --> 00:18:52.900
Thank you, Momo.

00:18:53.710 --> 00:18:57.470
I haven't done anything
to deserve your gratitude.

00:18:58.180 --> 00:19:00.350
You're so stubborn.

00:19:00.350 --> 00:19:01.970
That goes for you, too.

00:19:07.250 --> 00:19:08.740
This is goodbye.

00:19:11.660 --> 00:19:15.490
But I will see you again one day, won't I?

00:19:16.830 --> 00:19:18.760
Goodbye, until then.

00:19:19.760 --> 00:19:21.200
Yeah.

00:19:21.200 --> 00:19:25.140
And once you come back to life,
don't ever think of dying again.

00:19:25.140 --> 00:19:27.010
Never in a million years.

00:19:27.010 --> 00:19:28.500
I sure hope so.

00:19:29.670 --> 00:19:33.140
How come? Why are you so worried?

00:19:33.140 --> 00:19:36.680
Because everyone thinks you tried
to kill yourself...

00:19:36.680 --> 00:19:38.480
...over a broken heart.

00:19:38.950 --> 00:19:41.320
Even your crush knows about it.

00:19:43.150 --> 00:19:44.880
Ugh, that's so pathetic!

00:19:45.820 --> 00:19:49.450
I'll never be able to show my face
at school again! What'll I do?!

00:20:02.610 --> 00:20:05.380
I don't care if it looks pathetic...

00:20:05.380 --> 00:20:07.680
...because I get to stay alive!

00:20:17.790 --> 00:20:19.260
Where am I?

00:20:21.490 --> 00:20:24.190
What am I doing here?

00:20:28.770 --> 00:20:30.340
Mom...

00:20:30.340 --> 00:20:31.670
Sakura.

00:20:44.380 --> 00:20:47.320
I had a dream.

00:21:00.100 --> 00:21:01.330
Morning!

00:21:01.330 --> 00:21:02.200
Sakura!

00:21:02.200 --> 00:21:03.570
Good morning.

00:21:03.570 --> 00:21:07.000
A-ha. Maybe I'll cut my hair as short as yours.

00:21:07.240 --> 00:21:08.610
What?

00:21:08.610 --> 00:21:10.940
I had a little heart break, you see.

00:21:14.050 --> 00:21:16.010
But I'm okay now.

00:21:19.220 --> 00:21:20.750
Okay, pork cutlet bowl!

00:21:20.750 --> 00:21:21.290
Okay, pork cutlet bowl!

00:21:20.750 --> 00:21:21.780
Pork Cutlet Bowl

00:21:22.020 --> 00:21:24.110
Pork Cutlet Bowl
500 yen

00:21:26.960 --> 00:21:29.220
That was really fun the other day.

00:21:42.770 --> 00:21:44.240
It's snowing.

00:21:52.080 --> 00:21:54.570
She would've revived without our help.

00:21:57.690 --> 00:21:59.020
Probably.

00:21:59.020 --> 00:22:01.830
I can't believe you went and hung out with her.

00:22:01.830 --> 00:22:07.600
I want the souls I take away
to have lived life to the fullest.

00:22:07.600 --> 00:22:10.430
You are such a busybody, Momo.

00:22:12.670 --> 00:22:13.970
I can't help it, look.

00:22:15.340 --> 00:22:22.680
Peaceful souls are pure white,
like snow, and very pretty.

00:22:49.840 --> 00:22:55.370
Fukai nemuri kara umareta

00:22:55.980 --> 00:23:03.650
Watashi naze namida tomaranai darou

00:23:05.160 --> 00:23:12.930
Shiroi kami nabiku yasashii kaze

00:23:13.670 --> 00:23:20.000
Kotoba hitotsu, hitotsu omoi tsutau

00:23:21.810 --> 00:23:30.180
Watashi no mune de ikutsumo no inochi

00:23:30.720 --> 00:23:38.050
Hakanaku itoshiku keshite ku

00:23:38.520 --> 00:23:47.020
Yozora ni takaku shiroku mai odoru

00:23:47.370 --> 00:23:55.140
Kono hitomi sorasazu mimamoru
